Third-Party Software:
This tool is built on the nnU-Net framework (Isensee et al., 2021), which is licensed under Apache License 2.0 by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ). When redistributing images containing nnU-Net and/or its pretrained weights, users must comply with the Apache 2.0 license terms. See: https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet

Model Training & Validation:
The neuroblastoma segmentation model was trained and validated as described in:

- Veiga-Canuto D., Cerdá-Alberich L., et al. (2022). Comparative Multicentric 
  Evaluation of Inter-Observer Variability in Manual and Automatic Segmentation 
  of Neuroblastic Tumors in Magnetic Resonance Images. Cancers 14(15):3648. 
  https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers14153648

- Veiga-Canuto D., Cerdá-Alberich L., et al. (2023). Independent Validation of 
  a Deep Learning nnU-Net Tool for Neuroblastoma Detection and Segmentation in 
  MR Images. Cancers 15(5):1622. https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers15051622

